---
title: "Three endings"
note: "One setup, three films. A woman knocks on a strange door in a storm, and the door opens; then three scenes each continue that same clip (AFTER: the knock), as a sitcom, a horror film and a romance, each in a style of its own. One Generate renders all four clips; Orrery Film keeps every branch, so you can watch the same door open three ways. Her dog is cast as always: it trots through every ending, even the ones that forget to mention it. The storm and the house roll per seed."
tags: [h3, reel, branches, motion_context]
---
@h3 text 16:9
style: live-action, cinematic, one continuous shot
context: 22
$storm = {a howling gale|a downpour lit by lightning|wet snow driving sideways}
$house = {a crooked Victorian house on a hill|a lighthouse keeper's cottage on a cliff|a farmhouse at the end of a mud track}

CAST
@MAYA: a young woman in a yellow raincoat, soaked to the skin
@BISCUIT (always): her old grey greyhound, in a tartan dog coat

SCENE the knock
MUSIC: N/A
SHOT 7s: push in, slow
@MAYA runs through $storm up to the door of $house, @BISCUIT at her heels, and knocks three times. Nobody answers; then the lock clicks by itself.
@MAYA (a young woman's voice, out of breath): Hello? My car broke down…
SFX: the storm roaring; three heavy knocks; a lock clicking open
END ON: the door swings open on a dark hallway, and somewhere inside a light comes on

SCENE the sitcom
AFTER: the knock
style: a bright multi-camera sitcom, flat warm studio light, a laugh track
MUSIC: a bouncy slap-bass sting
SHOT 7s: static
The lights blaze on: the hallway is packed with strangers in party hats who shout "Surprise!" at the wrong person. @MAYA freezes, dripping, and someone hands her a slice of cake.
SFX: party horns; a studio audience bursting into laughter
END ON: @MAYA takes a bite of the cake and shrugs

SCENE the horror
AFTER: 1
style: a slow-burning horror film, deep shadows, cold blue moonlight, the grain of 35 mm film
MUSIC: a single low string note that will not resolve
SHOT 7s: push in, slow
@MAYA steps into the hallway. The light at the far end is a single candle, and as she reaches it the door slams shut behind her; in the dark, something breathes on the stairs above.
SFX: the storm cut off at once; a slow creak on each stair; breathing that is not hers
END ON: the candle goes out

SCENE the romance
AFTER: the knock
style: a warm romantic drama, golden firelight, soft focus, shallow depth of field
MUSIC: a gentle solo piano at a slow tempo
SHOT 7s: arc, slow
A man in a knitted jumper appears in the warm light with a towel over his arm, as surprised as she is. He hands her the towel; she laughs for the first time all night, and the fire crackles behind them.
SFX: a crackling fire; the storm muffled outside; soft laughter
END ON: the door closes on the storm, and the two of them stand by the fire
